# Pinterest guide - {{ title }}

Pinterest is a search engine: pins keep sending visitors for months. Aim for **3-5 fresh pins per day** across your product catalogue; for one product, start with **1 pin per day for 6 days**, then re-pin the winners.

You post pins yourself (Pinterest's developer rules also require a person to review each action).

## Setup (once)
1. Create a **Pinterest Business account** (free) and **claim your website/shop** so pins show your name.
2. Create 3-5 **boards** named with search keywords, e.g. `{{ copy.tags[0] }}`, `{{ copy.tags[1] }}`, `{{ copy.tags[2] }}`.
3. Fill your profile: keywords in the name and bio, a link to your shop.

